ck wants/h0/games/hack/playground, cribbage wants /h0/games/crib/criblog).Run `tools/measure_layout.py disk' for the current counts.  Mountthe same image as both /dd and /h0 and they all find their files:    OS9DISK=<this disk>  OS9H0=<this disk>  os9exec ...OS-9 filenames are case-insensitive, so /h0/games/hack/playgroundfinds GAMES/HACK/playground.Seven programs use SNOBOL4-in-C, a C library thatsimulates SNOBOL4's pattern matcher, with programs translated out ofGimpel's "Algorithms in SNOBOL4".  Each is an ordinary 68k program.The library and its makefile are in SRC/effo_snobol, the package's ownnotes in DOC/snobol.  blackjak, poker, rpoem, rstory, rstory2, stoneand tformat are the seven.larn resolves the same way: it wants /h0/GAMES/larn/PLAYGROUND, andGAMES/LARN/PLAYGROUND is on the disk.  It holds the scoreboard larnwrites there for itself, plus .larn.help, .lfortune and .larnmaze.larn plays: it lays out a level, shows its '?' help, keeps score andtakes commands.Those three data files came from the larn 12.2p4 sources; the binaryreports 12.0.  SOURCES.txt records where they came from.  Its siblingularn is complete and also runs.  gnuchessc and gnuan read their datafrom GNUCHESS4.0/MISC and both start.DOC/DEPENDS lists, per program, every absolute path its binarycarries -- read it before copying single commands elsewhere.See DOC/REBUILT-NOTES.md for four curated binaries that wereoverwritten during installation and what was done about each.------------------------------------------------------/dd/CMDS -- added utilities (356)------------------------------------------------------  agrep          grep that forgives spelling: `agrep -2 homogenos file' finds                 `homogeneous', allowing two letters wrong, missing or extra.                 -i ignores case, -w matches whole words, -c counts, -f reads                 patterns from a file, -d sets the record delimiter (`-d                 "^From "' for a mailbox)  a